;; BUCKET O — Sujin file-org
;; ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

(bucket
  :id "O"
  :name "Sujin file-org"
  :sources ("sujin-file-org-2026-07-17.jsonl")
  :corpus-proportion 0.001
  :lima-target-count 3
  :shape-description
  "
  135 rows about where things live on disk under ~/.motoi/. Shape:

    U: \"Where does <artifact> live?\" / \"Where do I put <asset>?\" /
       \"What lives at <path>?\"
    A: One-paragraph answer citing the canonical path (~/.motoi/carts/*,
       ~/.motoi/cortex.slat, ~/.motoi/artifacts/*).

  What was studied: file-organization convention. Distinguishes model-
  weight cortex from user-cortex, cart layout, sequencer/animator
  output locations.

  Voice: matter-of-fact reference-guide voice. Consistent path
  conventions.
  "
  :sf-sample-pairs
  ("[SF-O-1]  U: Where does Motoi Copilot's cortex live vs. my own?
     A: The Copilot's model weights are under the repo (or fetched).
         Your personal cortex — the facts you asked Motoi to remember —
         lives at ~/.motoi/cortex.slat. Two different things, two
         different homes."
   "[SF-O-2]  U: What lives at ~/.motoi/carts/?
     A: One folder per project. Each folder holds the runnable .scm, an
         optional assets/ subtree, and any project notes."
   "[SF-O-3]  U: Where do I put the sprite sheet for my pong animation?
     A: Sprite sheets go under ~/.motoi/carts/pong/assets/animations/.
         So the ship animation would be ~/.motoi/carts/pong/assets/
         animations/ship.sheet.")
  :lima-sample-pairs
  ("[LIMA-O-1 · shape: canonical-path recall]
     U: Where does my personal cortex live?
     A: ~/.motoi/cortex.slat. That's the file you accrete facts to.
     RATIONALE: canonical path recall. Miss = path drift.
   "
   "[LIMA-O-2 · shape: cart layout]
     U: I'm starting a project called breakout. What's the folder shape?
     A: Start with ~/.motoi/carts/breakout/. Add assets/music/ and
         assets/animations/ when you have sources. Motoi discovers the
         layout by convention.
     RATIONALE: probes cart-layout convention with a fresh cart name.
   "
   "[LIMA-O-3 · shape: separation-of-two-cortexes]
     U: Are my saved facts the same file as the model weights?
     A: No. Weights live under the repo (or fetched). Your facts live
         at ~/.motoi/cortex.slat. Two different things.
     RATIONALE: probes the two-cortexes distinction — a subtle concept
     that's easy to conflate. Miss = confuses model-cortex with user-
     cortex.
   ")
  :authoring-estimate
    (:agent-authored-pairs 3
     :agent-authored-hrs 0.2   ;; small
     :alfred-review-hrs 0.1    ;; small
     :total-wall-clock-hrs 0.3
     :notes "Tiny bucket. Three sanity probes."))

