;; SUMMARY — grand totals + recommendation
;; ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

(summary
  :total-lima-pairs 2000
  :per-bucket-target-sum
  "
  A:758  B:450  C:225  D:135  E:60   F:70   G:65   H:75
  I:30   J:25   K:30   L:30   M:20   N:5    O:3    P:17
  ────────────────────────────────────────────
  Sum: 1998 pairs (≈ 2000 with rounding)
  "
  :total-agent-hrs 53
  :total-alfred-review-hrs 17.4
  :total-wall-clock-hrs-serial 70.4
  :total-wall-clock-days-serial 4.5   ;; at 8h/day pace
  :total-wall-clock-days-parallel 2.5  ;; agent + Alfred run in parallel

  :recommended-authoring-sequence
  "
  ORDER by information-value-per-authoring-hour, front-load high-signal
  small buckets, back-load high-volume mixed buckets.

  Session 1 (small + high-signal):  G, J, N, M
    → 25 total pairs · ~5 hrs · gets voice + safety + reference nailed

  Session 2 (mid buckets):           I, K, L, O, P, F, E
    → 220 total pairs · ~11 hrs · fills mid-domain coverage

  Session 3 (chapter buckets):       C, D, H
    → 435 total pairs · ~14 hrs · book-take-root reveal

  Session 4 (big mixed):             A, B
    → 1,208 total pairs · ~25 hrs · large-volume authoring after
      voice-and-signal buckets are locked

  Alfred review runs concurrently in shorter batches, catching drift
  at each session boundary.
  "

  :surprises-flagged
  "
  1. Bucket M (\"Wave-3 refusal + Sakura-dip refusal\"): manifest says
     1,012 rows; direct count of train+valid+heldout is 12. The
     wave-3-refusal (2,577) and response-shape (2,081) source files
     were entirely stripped by safety-verify and template-threshold
     filters during v2 fold. LIMA can only probe the 12 surviving
     Sakura-dip minimalist refusals. IF Alfred intended for wave-3 to
     be in the corpus, that's a 2.0 SFT authoring signal, not a LIMA
     gap.

  2. Bucket P (\"Heldout untagged\"): methodology §2P intended this
     bucket for doctrine-memory probes authored from Alfred's memory
     index. The 1,000-row heldout is actually a CARVE-heldout eval-only
     cross-shape sample (mini-mirror of the corpus). Doctrine memories
     rode into training via bucket A's rollup and bucket J's persona
     waves — not via bucket P. Keep the 17 doctrine LIMA probes;
     mark them as diagnostic; do NOT use the 1,000-row heldout as a
     source for LIMA (it's eval-only).

  3. Bucket H's extension-glances sub-source (1,226 rows on Georg
     Jensen cuffs, Thonet chairs, Mathieson planes, ZFS filesystem
     etc.) is off-Motoi-voice, Sakura-adjacent operator-lookout
     material. It sits in the Motoi fold. This is a potential READ 4
     anti-pattern source: if it took root, Motoi could bleed into
     Sakura-shape operator glances. LIMA probes intentionally EXCLUDE
     this material — but Alfred should see it flagged.
  "

  :recommendation
  "
  Proceed with the 2,000-pair authoring plan per methodology §2 with
  three amendments:

  a. Bucket M: reduce target from 20 to ~5 pairs and mark as
     \"diagnostic — SFT substrate absent.\" Add a note to the READ 1
     rubric that recall on this bucket should be near-zero and that's
     expected under current v2 fold.

  b. Bucket P: keep 17 doctrine-memory probes but frame as cross-
     bucket-osmosis-diagnostic. Consider expanding to 40 to cover the
     full memory index if Alfred wants that reveal.

  c. Bucket H: EXCLUDE extension-glances from LIMA authoring.
     Consider it a READ 4 unprompted-emission source instead.

  Otherwise the corpus-proportional weave holds. Sample LIMA pairs
  above (48 total) are Alfred-eyeballable. If they read right, the
  full 2,000 authoring can begin. If any bucket's samples read wrong,
  we recalibrate that bucket's authoring shape before scaling up.
  "

  :next-steps
  "
  · Alfred eyeballs the 48 sample LIMA pairs above. Marks any that
    drift.
  · Alfred confirms the three amendments (M, P, H) or overrides.
  · Alfred says GO on authoring lanes.
  · Lacuna Eng dispatches authoring per the four-session sequence.
  · Alfred reviews at each session boundary.
  · Full 2,000-pair LIMA lands in ~3-5 days wall-clock.
  · LIMA trains on top of adapters.safetensors.
  · READs 1-4 run per methodology §3.
  · Reveal-report to Alfred + Jesse + David + Dare.
  ")

