;; ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
;; §section-cpt-mk2-outcomes-and-next-2026-07-21
;;
;; What actually happened 2026-07-21 after CPT completed:
;;
;; MEMORIZATION PROBE (the right CPT-layer test per literature):
;;   Base                : mean-word-jaccard 0.059, tpm mean 0.10
;;   SFT Weave (Mk 1)    : mean-word-jaccard 0.054, tpm mean 0.30
;;   CPT Weave (Mk 2)    : mean-word-jaccard 0.474, tpm mean 3.94, MAX tpm=80
;;   Per axis (CPT Weave training-terms hit ratio):
;;     Thinking  : 0.960  ← massive attach on propositional facts
;;     Sensation : 0.512
;;     Intuition : 0.498
;;     Feeling   : 0.350  ← thin attach on distributional/register content
;;
;;   Conclusion: the CPT data IS in there. LoRA r=128 SFT on top of the CPT
;;   adapter is a green-light bet — the substrate the SFT needs to retrieve
;;   from is demonstrably present.
;;
;; SFT CONFIG DECISION MADE 2026-07-21 (revised from LoRA r=128):
;;   Per C-LoRA research (arXiv:2502.17920) and CoT-SFT-overfitting research
;;   (arXiv:2501.09804) — smaller rank preserves CPT weights better and
;;   reduces overfitting risk. Adjusted from r=128 to r=32.
;;
;;   Full Mk 2 SFT recipe (85k pairs, 14 slices, research-backed):
;;     engineering/MK2-SFT-RECIPE-2026-07-21.ENG.slat  ← canonical
;;
;; SUPERSEDED-BY notice for the "LoRA r=128 recommended" line above:
;;   That was based on Mk 1's LoRA rank. Post-CPT research suggests r=32
;;   is better for preserving CPT-attached weights. See MK2-SFT-RECIPE
;;   for the full research-backed adjustments.


;; ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
;; §section-sft-doctrine-additions-2026-07-21
;;
;; Six new SFT-side doctrines established this session:
;;
;;   1. SFT MUST BE ABDUCTIVE (not declarative)
;;      Every pair shaped as: observation → candidate explanations → best-fit
;;      landing. Peirce's abduction is the meta-shape all pair templates sit
;;      inside. Declarative Q→A locks into phrase-surface overfit.
;;      Memory: [[sft-must-be-abductive-2026-07-21]]
;;
;;   2. AXES ARE AUTHORING, NOT TESTING
;;      The 4 Jung axes organize what we AUTHOR into the corpus. They are
;;      NOT a runtime behavior the model must exhibit. Do not probe per-axis
;;      response quality; probe kid-question capability at SFT layer.
;;      Memory: [[axes-are-authoring-not-testing-2026-07-21]]
;;
;;   3. NO SEALED CORPUS
;;      Training is global; injecting on axis X reshapes axes Y+Z+downstream.
;;      Design for differential attachment — some axes attach cleanly, others
;;      stay on base priors. Accept it as physics.
;;      Memory: [[no-sealed-corpus-2026-07-21]]
;;
;;   4. LLM FINE-TUNING IS ART, NOT SCIENCE (at our scale)
;;      Base training data is opaque (Qwen doesn't publish exact mix). No
;;      way to know optimal recipe. Trial-and-error is the actual method.
;;      Papers give priors, not proofs. Doctrine's value = repeatability +
;;      organization, not outcome prediction.
;;      Memory: [[llm-finetuning-is-art-not-science-2026-07-21]]
;;
;;   5. PHILOSOPHERS AS SFT PAIR SHAPES
;;      The 16 philosophers Motoi wove throughout the corpus each contribute
;;      a specific reasoning shape that becomes an SFT pair template. Not
;;      decoration — structural. 5 core weight-heavy (Peirce, Wittgenstein
;;      both, Jung, Lacan, Popper) + 10 woven as sub-shapes.
;;      Memory: [[philosophers-as-sft-shapes-2026-07-21]]
;;
;;   6. INTRINSIC-GRAPH SFT
;;      Graph relationships go INTO the pairs, not into runtime RAG. Every
;;      graph edge type (opposition, cross-ref, distributional-neighbor,
;;      cross-axis-bridge) becomes a pair template. Model knows the graph
;;      structure as internal fact, not lookup.
;;      Memory: (inside [[philosophers-as-sft-shapes-2026-07-21]] under Jung)
;;
;; Full recipe: engineering/MK2-SFT-RECIPE-2026-07-21.ENG.slat
